From: ionograms-handler
Subject: [PATCH] take the LO from the command line, not from a recompile

0012 moved the receive band by editing a literal in this file. That works and
it is what runs today, but it leaves the LO in two places -- here and
`center_freq` in `my_station.ini` -- with nothing to keep them equal.
`calc_ionograms` builds its downconversion mixer from the ini key (`f0=-cf`)
while the samples come from this line. A mismatch dechirps by the difference
and produces **empty products with no error in any log**. Nothing checks it and
nothing can: the LO is not written into the Digital RF metadata.

That is not a theoretical hazard. It blinded the station twice on 2026-08-19,
once by applying the ini before the recorder had been rebuilt and once by
editing this file and not rebuilding at all -- editing the source looks like it
changed the recorder.

So make the ini the only place the number lives, and let the launcher pass it.

**The mechanism already exists here and upstream wrote it.**
`examples/marieluise/w2naf.sh:29-36` reads a value out of the ini with an
inline `python3 - <<PY` that instantiates `chirp_config`, prints one attribute
and captures it into a shell variable, which the launcher then passes as
`--gps-lock-timeout`; the matching `po::value` sits three lines below the one
this patch adds. `--center-freq` is the same change in the same idiom, so this
introduces no new pattern into the program. 0015 is the launcher half.

The default stays `12.5e6`, which is what upstream tunes to at 25 MS/s, so a
bare invocation behaves exactly as before this patch.

**The new `std::cout` matters as much as the option.** Both incidents were
silent because a station on the wrong LO looks identical to a healthy one in
every log -- the products come out empty rather than wrong. Printing the LO and
the band it implies on every start makes the recorder state something that can
be compared against the ini without stopping anything, and gives the health
check something to read.

**This supersedes 0012**, which stays in the tree as the record of what ran
first. Do not apply both: 0012's hunk edits the same line and will not apply
after this one. Requires 0013 and the ini keys, exactly as 0012 did -- see the
note in README.md.

Applied against 0d27125, with 0012 already applied.

diff --git a/rx_uhd_ext_gps.cpp b/rx_uhd_ext_gps.cpp
